ield/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcf21feb-caad-5f01-82f0-e33663c8dbc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437328} {:answer/id #uuid "8328e87e-23da-585d-b66e-42111af5c87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8328e87e-23da-585d-b66e-42111af5c87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437329} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5477318-3d23-52d5-9a55-05595aeaea30" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55643e28-3c44-53e1-a6da-d559974acbda" :question/math-academy-id "q-103811" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all positive real numbers.\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, the statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$ So, $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$ Hence, statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049991 :topic/id #uuid "245d7b8c-ac58-53e1-bbb6-af3096067f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3567 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosecant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9d4f60c-cb6e-5f02-8f4a-a198f7cafa23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437336} {:answer/id #uuid "36efe75c-8338-5448-b8b1-f0f24de49042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d4f60c-cb6e-5f02-8f4a-a198f7cafa23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437336} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f359a76-6b4d-5ef4-8d92-7e15d488f261" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "434a0e71-1d31-5c13-a968-09b7e4ab49c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437338} {:answer/id #uuid "6e498609-ab5a-526b-bdc2-2b89a7e8bc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e498609-ab5a-526b-bdc2-2b89a7e8bc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437339} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e70be4-e476-5046-a564-3ee1193d0d78" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85984aac-915a-5905-a791-04f32942b8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437340} {:answer/id #uuid "4722da66-f024-52e9-b6dc-755aa8810cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4722da66-f024-52e9-b6dc-755aa8810cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437341} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cd87df-e0b6-57e0-879b-9a26805f19c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "048ceaff-1e4b-5807-8d50-fab96c1502f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103814" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function. $$\n- **II.** $x=9\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** The function takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/06/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050427 :topic/id #uuid "48167c86-51da-525c-908a-de3945756954" :topic/math-academy-id 3566 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a67b16f6-dc70-5d8b-9e47-2622982f487a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447672} {:answer/id #uuid "64620df8-e9fe-52ef-805c-2735ff596a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a67b16f6-dc70-5d8b-9e47-2622982f487a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447672} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c0c7e36-7fa6-5632-b634-da3ec87f60da" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5efab06-808a-55ce-99e2-98546c6701ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447674} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b73384-07ac-54b7-b92a-733a7793478e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5efab06-808a-55ce-99e2-98546c6701ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447674} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a69a867-51ee-5250-be62-b7dd01e44c96" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1a94dee-8c64-57f6-82ef-5179129198fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447676} {:answer/id #uuid "e0562874-5693-5737-bbd2-a529e3eaac2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0562874-5693-5737-bbd2-a529e3eaac2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447677} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4a53dfa-87de-5875-8f96-e8e1e35887fe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e25815e7-4d17-5965-b1f7-fc15c12bd9d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-103836" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- **II.** The domain of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\n- **III.** The period of the function is $\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](images/77/7785ad73f6e5212772c3053780ffd055f37cfb39927b6ddc3e40cd3a55b8ba4e.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The vertical asymptotes of the function are integer multiples of $\\pi $, i.e., $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The domain of the function is all real numbers except the values where the asymptotes occur, i.e., $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17