b/id #edb/ref 17592186438702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "340a8e11-ca0d-5e08-ab08-b9647c00e4dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-104049" :question/problem "![](images/51/5143df65d0f99c6511dc8ab13262831669c88535e19c986dacdb364e04847f58.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)\\ne f(2)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(2)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=2=f(2).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of the function doesn't have a break at $x=2$ and we can draw the graph of $f(x)$ around $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60efdf1c-df12-5856-aa4c-f4f6fc23d42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437348} {:answer/id #uuid "cea4be79-bc3f-5364-9f0f-d13cc3390e5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437349}] :answer-field