7592186438705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc9393f2-809c-5769-b329-186102da51c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-104051" :question/problem "![](images/65/65b9b32e8fac6a71141ce820855058367e9235129de7334db35a200905474cc0.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=5$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ exists\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=5$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(5)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{+}}f(x) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ doesn't exist\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function has a jump exactly at $x=5$\nand it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96e53957-3adf-512d-a153-562190ecd98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437354} {:answer/id #uuid "be515943-b831-586a-a2a6-0858894c576e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be515943-b831-586a-a