b/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3312f9fe-c2a1-5d75-b752-6c981a0a3f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104052" :question/problem "![](images/80/8086893e4587e68f8257b75f2070cf622fa141199d6bd8960f7c4fd8e7bcb349.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=0$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & =3, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=0.$ The graph contains a break at $x=0.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a2f64f-b3f7-5269-98a9-f17f1936fd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437360} {:answer/id #uuid "5aba2d92-17d5-581b-ba83-416e31577135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a2f64f-b3f7-5