d #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad98348d-cbe6-535a-9828-f9008c2ec2e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104124" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bdcfa35fb04028cbff32992b41214c878443d3815b676a0cf046f5a99bd771bd.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=-2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=f(-2)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-2$ and $f(-2)=5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{-}}f(x) & =5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=5=f(-2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050657 :topic/id #uuid "5cf444d7-d014-59c7-b47c-21b442662b58" :topic/math-academy-id 474 :topic/title "Left and Right Continuity"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f0646c-449a-55f7-a43e-10aed917f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461285} {:answer/id #uuid "6f47c9f4-cfdf-51cc-a8ee-2e312b6e2ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f0646c-449a-55f7-a43e-10aed917f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461285} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42517c5-86d0-573b-9c42-a43146a898c4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462396} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be579ceb-8f73-508e-8274-146cdc8bb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461287} {:answer/id #uuid "19f14dea-5bfb-587c-9cb9-670c75f65f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be579ceb-8f73-508e-8274-146cdc8bb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461287} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac105e7-89d8-52b0-b5e6-9803aa72f310" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd3708f-69c6-5fb0-a0c2-d6332aefe29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461289} {:answer/id #uuid "5df81d82-6062-53b0-8ac4-34d404968f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbd3708f-69c6-5fb0-a0c2-d6332aefe29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461289} :answer-field/id #uuid "4deab2df-6f34-5f4c-8d22-c93a07225cea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d00cc33e-d21d-57ae-828a-16fa83891b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-104357" :question/problem "![](images/30/30df82b4c47905fd8277067f9207a5e970a96d8ec386879d2872b5f5c3d8dd3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne 0=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 0=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050657 :topic/id #uuid "5cf444d7-d014-59c7-b47c-21b442662b58" :topic/math-academy-id 474 :topic/title "Left and Right Continuity"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7746b1d-22e8-5721-a847-a60ad72b51b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461291} {:answer/id #uuid "6f612c3f-7d07-5916-b27a-0ee2c0892bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #e