db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461435} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f0ca48-44d1-5bd6-9830-c490f17a2d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7edd4edd-c2bd-595e-87cd-340b998892bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461435} :answer-field/id #uuid "38dd7821-f0f2-5810-bd0f-71890d0ec23b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe40ba69-5c80-5288-8a8c-e5c1e0d1d354" :question/math-academy-id "q-105419" :question/problem "![](images/c7/c75313fbb97784b27ea0c57068e7221e0f9416ac4857b70723fd7ca949d9aba7.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)$\n- $x\\in [-3,\\infty )$\n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-3].$ It is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-3)$ and also left-continuous at $x=-3.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,0)$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=-3.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[-3,\\infty ).$ Although the function is continuous on $(-3,\\infty ),$ it is not right-continuous at $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d474031-aec8-57ab-a3e0-55a89435cf1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461437} {:answer/id #uuid "f7daefe6-fc8a-5e47-94be-0a48f56ddf85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7daefe6-fc8a-5e47-94be-0a48f56ddf85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461438} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0382769-e42c-58d2-b541-6e4e6dcc2ec8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2f5aa7e-d32d-5d0c-bdfe-e74efc085aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461439} {:answer/id #uuid "87addec4-73f4-5600-859d-f2a3ae0b54df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2f5aa7e-d32d-5d0c-bdfe-e74efc085aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461439} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a01675-4425-5843-ba6e-097451cce680" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c37fb727-928e-5d8e-8476-07eb63595218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461441} {:answer/id #uuid "73e840dd-1ac0-5de2-bcb8-fb0e704477a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73e840dd-1ac0-5de2-bcb8-fb0e704477a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461442} :answer-field/id #uuid "4899626b-7729-58f3-a88d-468c0c77f306" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9f390fe-da40-537a-ae87-c6dfb93153a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105423" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0<y\\le {x}^{3}}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-y<0}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-{x}^{4}<y<{x}^{4}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,16).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ab35358-6a6e-53c9-a359-2eeb55169a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461443} {:answer/id #uuid "01e83318-19e7-5daf-8d94-d46c64997a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e83318-19e7-5daf-8d94-d46c64997a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461444} :answer-field/id #uuid "40249fef-4857-5239-88aa-35f1ab209488" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462475} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9e5add6-21ff-5127-afaf-df7c753a3119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461445} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5aa1e0-c811-5a3c-9e71-6de7dd2c4260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9e5add6-21ff-5127-afaf-df7c753a3119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461445} :answer-field/id #uuid "058d3ef2-cefd-5d09-853d-5e64f8233ce5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462476} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491a04b5-b27e-564f-9f59-d114e4ce4441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461447} {:answer/id #uuid "d8df605e-3807-5915-bab0-6e1df41880af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491a04b5-b27e-564f-9f59-d114e4ce4441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461447} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3473981-d1e7-5830-8430-e252ede45aab" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d4a59fe-0871-5826-aa72-1fb9c0a2dad6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105431" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 6,\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 3}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\,1<{y}^{2}<16}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,-2\\le x\\le 2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,\\sqrt{3}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"} :activity/title "Open and Closed Sets" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409697} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409714}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8da227c0-43c3-53af-b829-2b5e45fe613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461449} {:answer/id #uuid "847d8a11-3b7f-5099-8561-09e695d74f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8da227c0-43c3-53af-b829-2b5e45fe613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461449} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d3162c5-3925-574f-b0da-e3491f823f6e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8880c6df-b262-5a08-9751-ccec61a1adfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461451} {:answer/id #uuid "c9119b74-7810-557e-b9ca-00afabe65407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9119b74-7810-557e-b9ca-00afabe65407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461452} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae4c6abe-cabb-5a92-afb6-9e51398743ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462479} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a95f0ca7-e174-5653-afa2-634c73938177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461453} {:answer/id #uuid "37738e30-2b54-557d-bee1-1f04ec248585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37738e30-2b54-557d-bee1-1f04ec248585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461454} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c4767ef-a476-5c1f-b66a-dae088dd8bb1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d461bff-0ae1-55fc-a03d-01dfa63c39ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-105437" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }x+y<4,\\,-1<x<4}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }0\\le x<4,\\,2<y\\le 4}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,2<y<4}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(-1,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049459 :topic/id #uuid "f6fd4776-56f0-5112-9cdc-83e344004d93" :topic/math-academy-id 2131 :topic/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc992ec-1afd-513d-b4a8-935bf11a1db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437414} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ae86bd-dc3b-5370-ab3b-9336719bd2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answ