 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56135889-753b-5df4-829a-e16e02adbe8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105692" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d0a06b24d18fac0e76a6d6f7cfc5409288c1b4dc7b1325d45b0ef30a8e3362f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has a curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/6c/6cb2333688e1a4a255398262d43046554c817705f09f7be9d6e6d082af519c42.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051085 :topic/id #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" :topic/math-academy-id 2132 :topic/title "The Curl of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d78c56-0653-549d-8fe9-e600bbc18e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437510} {:answer/id #uuid "7fda3753-247c-5e38-a385-69d3789ea1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d78c56-0653-549d-8fe9-e600bbc18e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437510} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46aee06-be1c-589d-8527-7c703976fa69" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc92ea1-396a-5412-b8bd-1b4004d4228c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437512} {:answer/id #uuid "0568e3f2-60bd-5c83-9d49-f6bb4d6708c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0568e3f2-60bd-5c83-9d49-f6bb4d6708c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437513} :answer-field/id #uuid "13972053-f581-5ed1-b4ad-918c440107af" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f38ae9-f0f2-572d-9185-5d097fca9a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437514} {:answer/id #uuid "2db0b74d-25fc-5ea3-b717-639ac2457432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db0b74d-25fc-5ea3-b717-639ac2457432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437515} :answer-field/id #uuid "04460364-e8a3-51e8-83a3-921fcf6f1abf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78a7026b-7d30-5e52-a908-0666dbeb58d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437516} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7bb458-d9d7-5e5c-bb23-6322f015cf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78a7026b-7d30-5e52-a908-0666dbeb58d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437516} :answer-field/id #uuid "472e5e59-acc9-5f2c-a05c-ad46e9a3685c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dbe3e81-bcac-55ba-b175-6059759ab5dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105695" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cc62b0a51519230bd1230874c00e17f165c345d11bc64e6d3c8fcf7788a5ee8.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is not irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into from the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6301b85-5d2c-56ff-84e2-115996719006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447754} {:answer/id #uuid "6506a1a7-c749-5ab8-bf45-811c20cd4ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6506a1a7-c749-5ab8-bf45-811c20cd4ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447755} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b2b4cdb-3abf-5f6f-bcdc-66b781648073" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4ec7a7a-e094-58ec-979e-c0bf24a2e267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447756} {:answer/id #uuid "f15882f0-4efb-540a-b88c-298befa6e513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f15882f0-4efb-540a-b88c-298befa6e513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447757} :answer-field/id #uuid "f993c988-d7c9-55e3-88e2-63e26e719b15" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfcc1904-da31-5d1f-88e5-643e150d439b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447758} {:answer/id #uuid "71bc7f39-96d2-5e6f-8f62-106eba0f95e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71bc7f39-96d2-5e6f-8f62-106eba0f95e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447759} :answer-field/id #uuid "6830e1f7-3853-5f1b-90ff-960bed912a23" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0880be83-dbd5-5dc8-a3cc-bdb045c80795" :question/math-academy-id "q-106684" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The  zero-matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $L.$\n- **II.** For any $A\\in L,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in L$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n- **III.** For any $A,B,C\\in L,$ we have $(A+B)-C=A+(B-C).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}=0.$ Hence, $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any matrix $A\\in L,$ there is a corresponding negative matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot 0=0,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any matrices $A,B\\in L,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n(A+B)-C=(A+B)+(-C)=A+(B+(-C))=A+(B-C).\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0372398e-98cc-5d0b-bd59-6907b71fcd7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447760} {:answer/id #uuid "09834786-19dd-511e-bc4b-325017903bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09834786-19dd-511e-bc4b-325017903bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447761} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5db8d1d-7cda-5388-9b50-1524815395c9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e973291-f4aa-5128-86d8-420bb8df5b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447762} {:answer/id #uuid "d953f2dc-43be-5437-ad88-4ff4ca6a36e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d953f2dc-43be-5437-ad88-4ff4ca6a36e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447763} :answer-field/id #uuid "85e3ef0b-5107-5857-9a4c-441585b50085" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abe910e-7792-5f04-8fb5-19de1bccf1cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447764} {:answer/id #uuid "fd608857-21d6-5979-a187-0dff4d75fdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0abe910e-7792-5f04-8fb5-19de1bccf1cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447764} :answer-field/id #uuid "e606421d-2ce0-54d0-8ffc-090b8e6bc46c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2555255-85b1-529f-85fb-94b6f9684401" :question/math-academy-id "q-106688" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The identity matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $S.$\n\n- **II.** For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n\n- **III.** There are matrices $A,B,C\\in S,$ such that $(A+B)+C\\ne A+(B+C).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=1.$ Hence, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\in S.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any matrix $A\\in S,$ there is a corresponding negative $2\\times 2$ matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot 1=1,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in S.$\n\n- Statement III is false. For any matrices $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have\n\n$$\n(A+B)+C=A+(B+C).\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fe9c763-05bb-5a4b-acbb-6d6d5b07b348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447766} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e69108-5b10-52f3-82f0-5f8cdd3daf36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe9c763-05bb-5a4b-acbb-6d6d5b07b348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447766} :answer-field/id #uuid "01e3522d-2e51-5c73-a8af-cf60ea62b81f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae645635-fdc9-5f4e-bbd3-9f767b2b1980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447768} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bf9c9c-34ad-596e-a213-50b843e0b77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6bf9c9c-34ad-596e-a213-50b843e0b77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447769} :answer-field/id #uuid "62892021-d450-5253-8370-c5ecb0c7ea15" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b50fdb2f-4826-56f1-afb9-3a2321c85e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447770} {:answer/id #uuid "e66e36b8-e92c-5769-bff0-59ef96ce8dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e66e36b8-e92c-5769-bff0-59ef96ce8dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447771} :answer-field/id #uuid "02e09a53-3ed5-504e-8a18-0de4f3b1d26e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f184570-b064-50c3-a82a-5d76cef8f98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106700" :question/problem "Let $M$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\begin{bmatrix}a & 1 \\\\ b & c\\end{bmatrix},$ where $a,b,c\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For any $A\\in M,$ we have $-A\\in M$ such that $A+(-A)=0.$\n- **II.** For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in M,$ we have $A+O=A.$\n- **III.** For any $A,B,C\\in M,$ we have $(A+B)+C=A+(B+C).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in M.$ Then $-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is the corresponding negative matrix such that $A+(-A)=O.$ However, $-{a}_{12}=-1\\ne 1,$ hence, $-A\\notin M.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the zero-matrix $O$ and any matrix $A\\in M,$ we have\n\n$$\nA+O=A\n$$\n\nsince $O$ is the unique zero element in the set of all matrices.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, For any matrices $A,B,C\\in M,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n(A+B)+C=A+(B+C)\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a60aa9c-b526-57f5-9921-6e034f4e04b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447772} {:answer/id #uuid "292b54e0-553a-546c-a133-cd314ddd54e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a60aa9c-b526-57f5-9921-6e034f4e04b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447772} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cda748e-5572-5f75-aaa2-5683fb3ee9ad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e1b53c2-7d8f-544e-9b4a-b476a4dc1c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447774} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1bf1e1-4ab7-5fed-978c-e7c1ab86b572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e1b53c2-7d8f-544e-9b4a-b476a4dc1c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447774} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac256d4c-c6d2-5f5f-9171-238a5e046e24" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8095d716-4ee4-5edf-994c-1b9f81d8cd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447776} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb60ae8-8e06-5d05-ab2b-75a2688d4313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceb60ae8-8e06-5d05-ab2b-75a2688d4313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447777} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a7a599-2463-57d2-a7d5-c52dad74ef02" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c35f03a5-0abf-5f24-a015-92c06eed08bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-106703" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is at most $10.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in T,$ we have $p(x)+0=0.$\n- **II.** For any $p(x),q(x)\\in T$, we have $p(x)+q(x)=p(x)-q(x).$\n- **III.** For any polynomial $p(x)\\in T$ we have $-p(x)\\in T$ such that $p(x)+(-p(x))=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}$ in $T.$ Then,\n\n$$\np(x)+0={x}^{2}+0={x}^{2}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)=q(x)={x}^{2}\\in T.$\nThen:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x)+q(x) & ={x}^{2}+{x}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2} \\\\ p(x)-q(x) & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p(x)+q(x)\\ne p(x)-q(x).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any polynomial $p(x)\\in T,$ there is a corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ such that\n\n$$\np(x)+(-p(x))=p(x)-p(x)=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(-p(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x))\\le 10,\n$$\n\nhence $-p(x)\\in T.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61500ddc-eba6-520e-a887-b48bc3ff18f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447778} {:answer/id #uuid "5584b906-d37d-5f15-9ec6-b8942a06abd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61500ddc-eba6-520e-a887-b48bc3ff18f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447778} :answer-field/id #uuid "3644870e-0c2d-5ee1-a9ad-63af23683a5b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60519578-6bbf-5170-bf83-14db96c9f9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447780} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3fa0d0-82f8-5210-896a-59fc58a32a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a3fa0d0-82f8-5210-896a-59fc58a32a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447781} :answer-field/id #uuid "733b49f6-094d-5040-86cc-dec4510b549e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "312dc01e-2c5b-55e3-94e8-5d2dbc027d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447782} {:answer/id #uuid "b41a99d3-c4b3-5fc7-a51f-b02c2727d79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b41a99d3-c4b3-5fc7-a51f-b02c2727d79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447783} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdbf6e1a-6a9e-5e00-b37b-25812a12873a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c34661b-de46-5e42-88de-7fe1ed369bf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-106710" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the set of all polynomials $p(x)$ such that $p(0)<0.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zero-polynomial belongs to $C.$\n- **II.** For any $p(x),q(x)\\in C,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$\n- **III.** The addition of polynomials in $C$ is associative." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $C$ contains only polynomials that evaluate to a negative number at $0.$ However, the zero-polynomial is *not* such a polynomial, as it equals $0≮0$ at $0.$ So, $0\\notin C.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in C,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in C,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)]\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481574} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481732}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying LU Factorizations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048743 :topic/id #uuid "ba8c9515-59e3-55c9-9d86-1de6e55c5474" :topic/math-academy-id 1779 :topic/title "LU Factorization of 2x2 Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56258d8c-e646-509a-8f28-9b491b3481fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461455} {:answer/id #uuid "09ef23d4-862d-578f-b427-bbae133ead4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ef23d4-862d-578f-b427-bbae133ead4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461456} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b2d6e88-66be-55b8-937a-f097cf9d0a8f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5b49c3-0779-557c-8921-65282b453bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461457} {:answer/id #uuid "68c311fa-d65a-5064-a5f2-843e88a9f3f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5b49c3-0779-557c-8921-65282b453bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461457} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fdefae0-1945-5459-8e2f-89ff965eadc8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c731b3-dbc9-5242-b984-177958f91d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461459} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd0f37d-448b-5552-acb3-dff3d5f8c125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c731b3-dbc9-5242-b984-177958f91d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461459} :answer-field/id #uuid "4715c2ce-c869-5eb5-8141-1dcbba399ac8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae199b8f-96fc-541b-8e00-25e26e1c8f40" :question/math-academy-id "q-106751" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{L}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}^{U}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying LU Factorizations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048743 :topic/id #uuid "ba8c9515-59e3-55c9-9d86-1de6e55c5474" :topic/math-academy-id 1779 :topic/title "LU Factorization of 2x2 Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe57a78b-d4ad-58a3-a332-1d5d1a41161f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461461} {:answer/id #uuid "ed276dc2-e752-5149-8daa-6a78dac6eb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe57a78b-d4ad-58a3-a332-1d5d1a41161f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461461} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad862c7-06d6-5d3e-9df8-9dc54efcf0c4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553c272d-3d3a-5260-bd9f-714a8605af98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461463} {:answer/id #uuid "4e234d92-1a15-5982-80b2-1a67952674f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e234d92-1a15-5982-80b2-1a67952674f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461464} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a44ba0a-420a-5ce8-9090-7717c7cae446" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2f54ad7-e111-5f33-a28c-2b1e1910a1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461465} {:answer/id #uuid "90d8b03d-a3ca-513c-a593-4303a50bda9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d8b03d-a3ca-513c-a593-4303a50bda9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461466} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e2bb08-94b2-5ba1-8d6a-ae59c5114f74" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02d764cc-1d89-57be-9543-a3cb1c6ba444" :question/math-academy-id "q-106756" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{L}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}^{U}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a914512e-7672-5333-8b5c-b71fba7518f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447790} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0cd5bb-20fe-5d02-8a73-e9965b60629a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a914512e-7672-5333-8b5c-b71fba7518f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447790} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd22bb13-41fa-5ad4-87ca-4ebdbb8f9c9c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8475cd02-dfa7-555e-8fe6-af9c1b3dfd1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447792} {:answer/id #uuid "0acd572a-df4e-5da4-ab5c-fa2488c8f02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0acd572a-df4e-5da4-ab5c-fa2488c8f02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447793} :answer-field/id #uuid "38a03ef7-085c-5065-a4eb-5d8739f0a73b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448936} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfc222dc-bcd7-58fe-b427-0f883e3ace51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447794} {:answer/id #uuid "2c767313-26ce-5c29-9d65-ec7d48a44dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c767313-26ce-5c29-9d65-ec7d48a44dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447795} :answer-field/id #uuid "0652d0f5-63c7-5c09-b3ab-489157c2a0ca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d83ac51c-0c75-5956-b55e-b6c1972a1661" :question/math-academy-id "q-106809" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a|x|,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For any $f(x)\\in N,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n- **II.** For any $f(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n- **III.** For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider $f(x)=|x|\\in N.$ Then,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot f(x)=(-1)\\cdot |x|=-|x|\\ne |x|.\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)\\cdot f(x)\\ne f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any function $f(x)\\in N$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 11" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547297} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548148}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "