:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447824} :answer-field/id #uuid "048ce3e7-4e91-5bdc-94ae-0dcff0516eac" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7243a9b-252c-5b36-9021-bf96acea16e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-107044" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{3},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly  independent\n- **II.** ${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent\n- **III.** ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}-({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot (-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}0+{x}_{2}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$  is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecb71f2b-1000-56b3-bbe6-687b5d590f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447826} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3ee093-657e-5024-8fec-edfa97116b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3ee093-657e-5024-8fec-edfa97116b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447827} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7a813e9-004c-5ceb-a7af-219f8f34da4b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daca64d4-1f39-5df2-bd12-569ab51b1741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447828} {:answer/id #uuid "91ce4987-96cc-5f80-bf18-867e10fb8c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daca64d4-1f39-5df2-bd12-569ab51b1741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447828} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a921d78-ac20-53d2-890f-ca83357fa944" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87a72c77-5b62-5c9c-8d2c-dce3236ea071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447830} {:answer/id #uuid "505c537f-ba45-5f50-8c2c-f79530d5a17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "505c537f-ba45-5f50-8c2c-f79530d5a17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447831} :answer-field/id #uuid "39119c3c-0c5e-55b4-aa93-6b38654a8ce2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "24ab3e85-383c-51f5-887f-f697f1697031" :question/math-academy-id "q-107045" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent\n- **II.** ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent\n- **III.** ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1})+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}){v}_{1}+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot {v}_{2}+1\\cdot (-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},-{v}_{1}}$  is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Indeed,  if this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot {v}_{2}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1b10e9b-bcf4-5130-85fc-49053cfefdbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447832} {:answer/id #uuid "475086cf-f02f-5e8a-a4a2-fa006f64dc42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "475086cf-f02f-5e8a-a4a2-fa006f64dc42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447833} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa301ff6-54cb-598d-bef1-558bf2aba10f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448956} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a60576b-e768-5815-9199-10025a9ffb26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447834} {:answer/id #uuid "3c33f922-fd87-5120-a935-f4f1b6089257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a60576b-e768-5815-9199-10025a9ffb26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447834} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97d3d50-a922-51ec-9905-e992f040dac9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4854c555-72a3-55eb-8878-f93699e6e4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447836} {:answer/id #uuid "e5fb77dc-2d83-5c4c-afe5-7ba222ae8083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fb77dc-2d83-5c4c-afe5-7ba222ae8083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447837} :answer-field/id #uuid "230a8bc2-029d-5dd9-b388-e30b57477b91" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "931e27f9-e2c3-59ee-b477-76a2f89436c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-107048" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${2{v}_{1},-3{v}_{2},4{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent\n- **II.** ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent\n- **III.** ${-{v}_{1},-{v}_{2},-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}(-3{v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(4{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+(-3{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+(4{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1},-3{v}_{2},4{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {v}_{1}+3\\cdot {v}_{2}+1\\cdot (2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}(2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, suppose\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}(-{v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, implies that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+(-{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+(-{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,  since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, it\nmust be ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$  Therefore, the set \n${-{v}_{1},-{v}_{2},-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd9a0fe4-bfa2-56e7-a7aa-c4e159871228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447838} {:answer/id #uuid "11759683-1e2b-57c5-acc7-365876e7e0f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11759683-1e2b-57c5-acc7-365876e7e0f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447839} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3bf5a04-3210-53b6-ad7c-70f653ed90c0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1f691af-5f0b-5b15-b9bc-564c36baef22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447840} {:answer/id #uuid "201b20b7-5ad4-5939-ac65-7e345d5b2f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201b20b7-5ad4-5939-ac65-7e345d5b2f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447841} :answer-field/id #uuid "68c44f75-03af-5a93-923c-e314211b8cb8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e57efc68-7759-5515-b49f-34d955643d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447842} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2bccf7-8ef1-5d06-9e23-35ef50275551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2bccf7-8ef1-5d06-9e23-35ef50275551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447843} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e768dc1-fa17-5741-b585-8f3904940f23" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfbc38a5-7760-5f24-838d-7ab05bc650ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447844} {:answer/id #uuid "d86ff6e7-6390-5064-ab32-ae7f45a24bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfbc38a5-7760-5f24-838d-7ab05bc650ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447844} :answer-field/id #uuid "25d9e8de-1ec5-57ba-a22e-d5b899f78a21" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3056b610-3deb-5e11-aff8-96abed8c674b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107102" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{5}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $a{t}^{5}+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\n- **II.** $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{5}[t]$\n\n- **IV.** $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{5}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{5}+{b}_{1}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{5}+{b}_{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{5}+{b}_{1})+({a}_{2}{t}^{5}+{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{5}+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=a{t}^{5}+b$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =k(a{t}^{5}+b) \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{5}+(kb),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b08e73-1f97-5a9d-8765-011794989893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447846} {:answer/id #uuid "379c45bd-fa59-5ece-ab64-9afffcac34e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "379c45bd-fa59-5ece-ab64-9afffcac34e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447847} :answer-field/id #uuid "35bdfd88-d00a-5ed9-a68f-ca51b0ce0895" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022db60e-534a-5da4-a8ce-2262d162b252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447848} {:answer/id #uuid "383bebdb-aec6-525b-b673-e79f4e15fcf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "383bebdb-aec6-525b-b673-e79f4e15fcf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447849} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de82b26-9be4-5035-a6ca-876c1fd4828c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448964} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7df5afee-6009-5f5b-a9c2-646fb00b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447850} {:answer/id #uuid "26dcbaa9-c2b0-5802-846a-d21c04bfbc1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26dcbaa9-c2b0-5802-846a-d21c04bfbc1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447851} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa12072-bf91-5f0f-841d-56cc29970264" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13152dab-7851-553c-a5a9-bca0408871b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447852} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ca9956-b7f2-56a5-955d-23824a527303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13152dab-7851-553c-a5a9-bca0408871b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447852} :answer-field/id #uuid "343e3cc5-810f-59a1-a98a-5a44697db1ca" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f27a4a5-4686-5577-a411-11aa97fab74a" :question/math-academy-id "q-107112" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a\\in R\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n\n- **II.** $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\n- **IV.** $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{bmatrix}$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & -ka\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af81d6e6-3cad-5c8a-99a9-13bc107158af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447854} {:answer/id #uuid "4921fc50-ffd5-5037-85e5-4437f4da71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4921fc50-ffd5-5037-85e5-4437f4da71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447855} :answer-field/id #uuid "31478e71-bb60-536e-8adc-4001942eec0d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7871ce40-048e-5347-b7c4-782324459d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447856} {:answer/id #uuid "54e54e39-08f5-53d6-b847-857578e17e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e54e39-08f5-53d6-b847-857578e17e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447857} :answer-field/id #uuid "19481cce-f1a9-5f87-8a34-93aac01ae946" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5f3b98c-c4eb-5c6c-ace2-f7e5a2fd7de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447858} {:answer/id #uuid "3b35c2e7-4cc8-5a23-9d0a-9ee7e8200d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b35c2e7-4cc8-5a23-9d0a-9ee7e8200d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447859} :answer-field/id #uuid "e99ca2b0-1668-5738-9b06-76be8f1daed7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} {:answer/id #uuid "fc911407-1e5d-58b7-8982-c859119fe356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b988c1-5329-5cf2-9e2b-7bef7867ab8c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89286e95-724b-57e9-aee8-7d71e484cafb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107113" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495500} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496337}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id